  "title": "Affection & Inclination towards Non-Believers",
  "data": "From many Qur'anic verses and traditions, we can conclude that a Muslim should keep clear of showing love to, sharing affection with, and inclining towards the non-believers, as well as of imitating them and following their ways. In this respect, Allah the All-exalted says (in the Holy Qur'an):\nقَدْ كَانَتْ لَكُمْ اُسْوَةٌ حَسَنَةٌ فِىْۤ اِبْرٰهِيْمَ وَالَّذِيْنَ مَعَهٗ اِذْ قَالُوْا لِقَوْمِهِمْ اِنَّا بُرَءَاۤؤُ مِنْكُمْ وَمِمَّا تَعْبُدُوْنَ مِنْ دُوْنِ اللّٰهِ\nQAD KAANAT LAKUM USWATUN HASANATUN FEE IBRAAHEEMA WAL LADHEENA MA'AHOO IDH QAALOO LIQAWMIHIM INNAA BURA'AA'U MINKUM WA MIMMAA TA'BUDOONA MIN DOONILLAAH\nIndeed, there is for you a good example in Ibrahim and those with him, when they said to their people: Surely we are clear of you and of what you serve besides Allah;\nكَفَرْنَا بِكُمْ وَبَدَا بَيْنَنَا وَبَيْنَكُمُ الْعَدَاوَةُ وَالْبَغْضَاۤءُ اَبَدًا\nKAFARNAA BIKUM WA BADAA BAYNANAA WA BAYNAKUMUL A'DAAWATU WAL BAGHDAA'U ABADAA\nwe declare ourselves to be clear of you, and enmity and hatred have appeared between us and you forever. (60:4)\nShaykh al-Saduq has reported Imam al-Sadiq (a.s.) as saying, “Almighty Allah revealed to one of His prophets to convey this message to the believers: Do not dress in the clothing of My enemies, do not eat what they eat, and do not behave as they behave, lest you become My enemies as they are.”\nIn view of this, traditions have forbidden certain acts for no other reason than to avoid imitating the non-believers."
}
